# What the packaging build context is allowed to carry.
#
# Not tidiness: build/ holds the 133 MB staged tree from the last local package
# build and .pio holds an entire toolchain's output, and docker uploads the
# whole context to the daemon before reading the first line of the Dockerfile.
# An unfiltered context here is minutes of copying, per architecture, to send
# files the build then ignores.
#
# image/ is deliberately *not* excluded: the flashable firmware goes into the
# package. See packaging/docker/Dockerfile.package-builder.
build*/
dist/
.pio/
.git/
.venv/
**/.venv/
**/__pycache__/
**/*.egg-info/
site/
emulation/
sim/
.devcontainer/
robot_output.xml
log.html
report.html
